{
 "name": "V02-is-the-law-in-force-EN",
 "cards_dir": "v02/en",
 "out": "v02",
 "captions": [
  {
   "id": "c1",
   "text": "Sri Lanka passed a data protection law in 2022. So is it in force?"
  },
  {
   "id": "c2",
   "text": "Partly — and the “partly” matters."
  },
  {
   "id": "c3",
   "text": "The regulator, the Data Protection Authority, has existed since 2023."
  },
  {
   "id": "c4",
   "text": "The duties on businesses start on the first of January 2027."
  },
  {
   "id": "c5",
   "text": "Have a lawful reason. Tell people what you collect. Keep it safe. Report leaks."
  },
  {
   "id": "c6",
   "text": "Your rights to see, correct or delete your file? Written into the Act. But no start date."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7",
   "text": "Same for the marketing-message rules, and the fines."
  },
  {
   "id": "c8",
   "text": "You may have read it all started on 18 March 2025. That date was cancelled four days before it arrived."
  },
  {
   "id": "c9",
   "text": "We track every section at datasavi.lk."
  }
 ],
